  "training": {
    "hints": [
      "Run, then Start once. The batch picks, carries and places all four cartons, restaging from the carton-load supply after each home return.",
      "X, Y and Z encoder-count tags are simulated plant feedback, zeroed at the pickup/home pose and scaled at 10 counts/mm. A PLC comparison rung requires every axis to be within ±5 mm before accepting Start.",
      "A 750 ms pickup dwell enables vacuum. The CTU counts a completed placement plus home return, not elapsed time alone.",
      "Machine Stop, System Enable loss, pallet-permissive loss, or the simulated training trip clears every axis command and requires a fresh Start. Machine Reset returns the plant and PLC sequence to home."
    ],
    "solution": {
      "summary": "This is an original functional reference for the control concept, not a copy of the photographed solution.",
      "steps": [
        "Trace System Enable, Start, Stop, Reset, simulated trip, pallet permissive and measured feedback in Main.",
        "Inspect the X, Y and Z calls to FB_AxisDrive and the vacuum call to FB_VacuumGripper; each FB call has its own instance DB.",
        "Follow sequence_step and the encoder comparisons that create the six independent axis-direction commands."
      ],
      "acceptance": "A carton is picked only at home and placed only at a valid pallet position."
    },
    "assetRequirements": [
      "XY gantry",
      "pallet magazine",
      "carton load",
      "supported pickup table"
    ],
    "machineGuide": {
      "purpose": "Four-carton palletizing lesson: one Start runs a complete gantry batch with simulated encoder feedback, PLC-commanded vacuum, placement feedback and home return.",
      "startConditions": [
        "Select the built-in offline controller; no PLC connection is required.",
        "System Enable and pallet permissive are true, simulated trip is clear, the pickup carton is present, and all measured axes are home."
      ],
      "normalSequence": [
        "Run, then press Start once to begin the four-carton batch.",
        "After each home return, the carton-load supply stages the next carton at the supported pickup station until all four positions are filled.",
        "The gantry lowers onto the carton, dwells 750 ms, picks up, carries to the next pallet slot, releases on the pallet, and returns home.",
        "The layer-complete lamp follows the fourth completed home return. The X/Y/Z encoder-count watch values track simulated position relative to pickup home."
      ],
      "stopBehavior": [
        "Machine Stop freezes pose and attachment, clears all six axis commands and vacuum, and preserves the PLC sequence step and placed cartons. Fresh Start resumes; app Run alone does not.",
        "System Enable loss, pallet-permissive loss, or simulated trip removes the machine seal-in. Clear the cause and press Start. Machine Reset clears the sequence/count and restores the preloaded home plant."
      ],
      "faultBehavior": [
        "Opposed axis commands, actuator commands without pallet permission, or vacuum loss away from a supported place latch a modeled plant fault. Machine Reset restores the lesson. The safety-trip input is instructional only, not a safety-rated function."
      ],
      "expectedObservations": [
        "The pickup carton remains on a table until attached. Carried cartons follow the tool; released cartons remain on four separate pallet slots.",
        "Encoder counts change with simulated travel. Home is generated from the completed return; the placement counter advances after release and home return."
      ]
    },
